From 8cf922af398b9ada8cdc02ce0f912270e6aa837e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Duttke <jens@duttke.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:10:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/vc1_parser: give frames without pulldown flags two
 field periods

Since e930b834a9 (lavf: use AV_CODEC_PROP_FIELDS where appropriate),
libavformat times VC-1 in field periods: a packet lasts
(1 + repeat_pict) / (2 * framerate). The parser sets repeat_pict = 1
for a frame only when the sequence header has the broadcast flag set,
and leaves it at 0 otherwise, so every frame of a stream without
pulldown flags is timed as a single field and raw elementary streams
play at twice their rate. The H.264 and MPEG-1/2 parsers were adjusted
in that commit; the VC-1 parser was not.

An interlaced 25 fps PAL stream (Kanu_720_576_25_interlaced.vc1, 220
frames) was timed at 20 ms per frame and lasted 4.4 s instead of 8.8 s;
a 29.97 fps one (Ice_720_480_2997_interlaced.vc1) at 16.7 ms per frame.
With the fix they are timed at 40 ms and 33.4 ms. Broadcast streams
with 3:2 pulldown keep their 33.4/50 ms cadence, and fate-vc1 passes
unchanged.
---
 libavcodec/vc1_parser.c | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1_parser.c b/libavcodec/vc1_parser.c
index 595d066dea..65ade1aa6c 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vc1_parser.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1_parser.c
@@ -93,10 +93,11 @@ static void vc1_extract_header(AVCodecParserContext *s, AVCodecContext *avctx,
         else
             s->pict_type = vpc->v.s.pict_type;
 
+        // A frame lasts two field periods, the unit lavf times VC-1 in
+        // since it marks the codec with AV_CODEC_PROP_FIELDS.
+        s->repeat_pict = 1;
+        // Pulldown flags are only valid when 'broadcast' has been set.
         if (vpc->v.broadcast){
-            // process pulldown flags
-            s->repeat_pict = 1;
-            // Pulldown flags are only valid when 'broadcast' has been set.
             if (vpc->v.rff){
                 // repeat field
                 s->repeat_pict = 2;
@@ -104,8 +105,6 @@ static void vc1_extract_header(AVCodecParserContext *s, AVCodecContext *avctx,
                 // repeat frames
                 s->repeat_pict = vpc->v.rptfrm * 2 + 1;
             }
-        }else{
-            s->repeat_pict = 0;
         }
 
         if (vpc->v.broadcast && vpc->v.interlace && !vpc->v.psf)
-- 
